Summary:

A critical security alert was triggered by suspicious HTTP POST traffic originating from external IP address 107.191.58.76 and targeting the internal Microsoft SharePoint server SharePoint01 (172.16.20.17). The request targeted /_layouts/15/ToolPane.aspx?DisplayMode=Edit&a=/ToolPane.aspx, with a spoofed or suspicious Referer header pointing to /_layouts/SignOut.aspx and a content length of 7699 bytes.

The observed activity is consistent with attempted exploitation of CVE-2025-53770, known as ToolShell, which involves unsafe deserialization and can result in remote code execution on vulnerable on-premises SharePoint Server deployments.

The investigation determined that the traffic was malicious, the attack was assessed as successful, and the HTTP response code was reported as 200. The incident was classified as a True Positive and requires escalation to Tier 2 for further investigation, containment, eradication, and impact assessment.

